  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nA large upper ridge over the western U.S. will become firmly\nestablished over the weekend. This will lead to mainly dry and hot\nweather conditions. With Saturday now one day away and the\nconsistent forecast for at least major heat impacts this weekend,\nwill upgrade the Extreme Heat Watch to Extreme Heat Warning for\nSaturday through Sunday. Highs on Saturday will be near 100 in\nmost areas and highs on Sunday will be above 100 in most areas.\nLows Sunday morning will be 65 to 70 in most areas. In addition, \nthis heat wave will be more humid than usual, especially in the \nnortheastern zones where dew points are expected to remain in the \n60s. These prolonged conditions may raise risk for heat related \nillnesses.\n\nAdditionally, ensemble guidance is pointing to breezy conditions\nSunday afternoon with southerly wind gusts potentially greater \nthan 30 mph. If this occurs in the presence of humidity in the \nteens and 20s, near critical fire weather conditions may emerge \nfor parts of the area. Recent precipitation and green fuels may \nlimit the overall extent of the risk, but this period remains \nworth monitoring.\n\nA cold front Sunday night will cool temperatures somewhat early \nnext week with highs mainly in the 90s on Monday and 80s north and\n90s south on Tuesday. Precipitation chances begin Tuesday night\nand continue at times the remainder of next wee. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNo deviations were made to the NBM. Ensembles are in line with \ngood consensus for the hot and dry weather this weekend with above\naverage confidence. Even if forecast maximums come in below \nexpectations, the humid air mass would offset that moderation. \nAdditionally, the combination of hot and humid conditions with \nlittle overnight recovery leave enough justification to keep the \nmessaging going.",
